ortability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.675,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The module passed 3 of 3 standalone runs right after, at the same load'","AC2: 'synthetic CPU load that previously reproduced the failure'","No load harness, run count, or pre-fix failure rate is stated anywhere in the plan."],"finding":"AC2's proof references a 'synthetic CPU load that previously reproduced the failure', but the plan documents no such reproduction. The only observed failure was inside a full `make verify` at load ~44. The Context reports the module passed 3 of 3 standalone runs at that same load. The before/after proof is therefore unspecified and may not discriminate fixed from unfixed code.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c20f1f7596238eb","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC2: 'The module passes under synthetic CPU load that previously reproduced the failure.'","norm_id":"nab20e9f93df35ca7","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer runs the module 3 times under some load, it passes as it already did before the fix, and AC2 is ticked without proving anything.","The flake recurs in `make verify` because the synthetic load never matched the conditions that triggered it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a deterministic check that does not depend on load. Either record `git_fetch._GIT_TIMEOUT` (or the timeout passed to the git subprocess) during the recovery `materialize` call and assert it is not `_BOUND_S`, or assert it equals the module default. If keeping a load-based AC, name the harness (for example, N busy-loop processes equal to 2x CPU count), the run count, and the observed pre-fix failure rate.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_s