ed","decision_margin":-0.6625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: 'the `slow_ls_tree` fixture also monkeypatches `git_fetch._GIT_TIMEOUT` to `_BOUND_S` (1 second) for the whole test'","Title/AC1 target only `test_build_with_timed_out_listing_writes_no_sidecar`, while AC2 targets the whole module"],"finding":"The plan scopes the fix to one test, but the root cause it names is the shared `slow_ls_tree` fixture capping `_GIT_TIMEOUT` 'for the whole test'. It does not say whether other tests in the module that use this fixture also make real git calls under the 1s cap. AC2 requires the whole module to pass under load, so any such test would leave AC2 unmet.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0dc12e8fc922776c","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem; AC2 ('The module passes')","norm_id":"n3140e6aa4026501e","priority":0.1375,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A sibling test using `slow_ls_tree` runs real git after disabling the slow wrapper and still flakes under load"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Fix the decoupling in the fixture itself, so `slow_ls_tree(False)` restores `_GIT_TIMEOUT`. That covers all users of the fixture uniformly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale"