_not_bound_by_the_slow_path_budget`, simulates a slow host with a fixed `sleep 2` in the git wrapper (`WHIPPET_LOADED`), not with CPU load. So no artifact shows that the CPU load reproduced the failure before the fix or that the module passes under it after.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8e18ea80c3a794db","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC2 ('The module passes under synthetic CPU load that previously reproduced the failure')","norm_id":"n03ab61e1f0e7d477","priority":0.1833,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or CI maintainer tries to confirm AC2 and finds no recipe to rerun it","The fixed `sleep 2` stand-in proves the limit is restored, but it does not show that the original CPU-load failure is gone. A sibling test that still applies the 1-second limit to the whole test (e.g. `slow_git` in test_snapshot_git_watchdog_d33f.py:60) would go unnoticed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword AC2 to 'A regression test (`test_recovery_listing_is_not_bound_by_the_slow_path_budget`) makes the recovery `ls-tree` answer after 2s and passes; it fails if the 1s limit leaks into the recovery call'. Alternatively, add the exact CPU-load reproduction command with its before (fail) and after (pass) results.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod